# Miru Browser - iOS Development Rules

## Project Overview

This is an iOS browser app built with Swift and SwiftUI targeting iOS 26+. It includes:
- Main app target: `Miru Browser`
- Share Extension target: `Share Extension`
- Bundle identifier: `miru.Miru-Browser`
- URL scheme: `miru://`

## Building and Running in Simulator

### Prerequisites
- Xcode must be installed with iOS Simulator support
- Command line tools: `xcodebuild`, `xcrun simctl`

### Step 1: Boot the iOS Simulator

```bash
# Boot iPhone 17 Pro simulator (or another available device)
xcrun simctl boot "iPhone 17 Pro"
open -a Simulator
```

To list available simulators:
```bash
xcrun simctl list devices available
```

### Step 2: Build the App

Build using xcodebuild from the project root:

```bash
cd "/Users/kevindutra/Code/Miru Browser"
xcodebuild -scheme "Miru Browser" \
  -configuration Debug \
  -destination "platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro" \
  -derivedDataPath build \
  build
```

The built app will be at: `build/Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/Miru Browser.app`

### Step 3: Install and Launch

```bash
# Install the app on the booted simulator
xcrun simctl install booted "build/Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/Miru Browser.app"

# Launch the app
xcrun simctl launch booted "miru.Miru-Browser"
```

### Step 4: Test URL Scheme

Open a URL in the browser:
```bash
xcrun simctl openurl booted "miru://open?url=https://apple.com"
```

### Taking Screenshots

```bash
xcrun simctl io booted screenshot "screenshot.png"
```

## Troubleshooting

### Simulator Frozen or Unresponsive

Kill and restart the simulator:
```bash
xcrun simctl shutdown all
killall Simulator 2>/dev/null
sleep 2
xcrun simctl boot "iPhone 17 Pro"
open -a Simulator
```

### Build Fails with Disk Space Error

Clean the build directory:
```bash
rm -rf build/
```

Also consider cleaning Xcode's DerivedData:
```bash
rm -rf ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/Miru*
```

### Swift Type Errors with ShapeStyle

When using ternary operators with SwiftUI styles like `.primary` and `.secondary.opacity()`, 
use explicit `Color` types to avoid type mismatches:

```swift
// Bad - causes type mismatch error
.foregroundStyle(isDisabled ? .secondary.opacity(0.4) : .primary)

// Good - explicit Color types
.foregroundStyle(isDisabled ? Color.secondary.opacity(0.4) : Color.primary)
```

## Project Structure

```
Miru Browser/
├── Miru_BrowserApp.swift       # App entry point with URL handling
├── ContentView.swift           # Main browser view with empty state
├── Info.plist                  # URL scheme configuration
├── Views/
│   ├── WebView.swift           # WKWebView wrapper
│   ├── NavigationBar.swift     # Bottom navigation toolbar (glass effect)
│   ├── SettingsView.swift      # Settings sheet
│   ├── ShareSheet.swift        # Share functionality
│   └── SwipeToCloseModifier.swift
├── Services/
│   ├── AdBlocker.swift         # Content blocking manager
│   ├── FilterListParser.swift  # EasyList format parser
│   └── FilterUpdateService.swift # Background filter updates
├── Models/
│   ├── BrowserState.swift      # Observable browser state
│   └── Settings.swift          # App settings
└── Resources/
    └── easylist.txt            # Bundled EasyList filter rules
```

## Key Commands Reference

| Action | Command |
|--------|---------|
| List simulators | `xcrun simctl list devices available` |
| Boot simulator | `xcrun simctl boot "iPhone 17 Pro"` |
| Shutdown simulator | `xcrun simctl shutdown all` |
| Build app | `xcodebuild -scheme "Miru Browser" -configuration Debug -destination "platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro" -derivedDataPath build build` |
| Install app | `xcrun simctl install booted "build/Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/Miru Browser.app"` |
| Launch app | `xcrun simctl launch booted "miru.Miru-Browser"` |
| Terminate app | `xcrun simctl terminate booted "miru.Miru-Browser"` |
| Open URL | `xcrun simctl openurl booted "miru://open?url=https://example.com"` |
| Screenshot | `xcrun simctl io booted screenshot "output.png"` |

## Notes

- Always request `["all"]` permissions when running xcodebuild or simctl commands
- The build requires network access for some Swift package dependencies
- iOS 26.1/26.2 simulators are available (iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17, iPhone Air, iPads)

